{"version": 2, "width": 96, "height": 36, "timestamp": 1791304276, "idle_time_limit": 2.0, "command": "node scripts/demo/analyst.mjs", "title": "darktrace-mcp / analyst / synthetic mock", "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/zsh"}}
[0.039361, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H\u001b[1;36mDARKTRACE MCP  /  02 / INVESTIGATE\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mSynthetic local appliance • no production data\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nClaude Code • read profile\r\n\r\n"]
[0.039474, "o", "$ claude --mcp-config <temporary mcp.json> --strict-mcp-config -p \"…\"\r\n"]
[0.039495, "o", "\r\n> Which devices and model breaches are visible? What should I investigate next?\r\n"]
[0.039511, "o", "\r\n"]
[3.30657, "o", "\r\n"]
[3.306584, "o", "I'll pull the device list and recent model breaches in parallel.\r\n"]
[3.83512, "o", "\u001b[36mMCP → darktrace_get_devices\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.83518, "o", "{\"operation\":\"get_devices\",\"query\":{\"count\":50,\"includetags\":true}}\r\n"]
[3.85933, "o", "\u001b[32m  ← tool result received\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.859411, "o", "\r\n"]
[4.537784, "o", "\u001b[36mMCP → darktrace_list_model_breaches\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.537849, "o", "{\"operation\":\"get_modelbreaches\",\"query\":{\"minimal\":true,\"includeacknowledged\":true}}\r\n"]
[4.549149, "o", "\u001b[32m  ← tool result received\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[8.820139, "o", "\r\n"]
[8.820168, "o", "Devices: one returned, sarah-desktop-12 (did 230, Apple desktop,\r\n10.0.18.224, labelled \"Sarah Development\", with a quarantine timestamp).\r\n"]
[8.82017, "o", "\r\n"]
[8.820206, "o", "Model breaches: one returned, pbid 123, \"Anomalous Connection::1 GiB\r\nOutbound\" (Critical, score 44%). Device fs182 (did 96, server) sent about\r\n1.16 GiB outbound against a 1 GiB threshold. The breach has two comments.\r\n"]
[8.820209, "o", "\r\n"]
[8.820252, "o", "Next steps:\r\n- Read the two comments on pbid 123 for prior analyst context.\r\n- Pull connection details for did 96 around the breach time to see the\r\n"]
[8.820276, "o", "  destination of the outbound transfer.\r\n- Check why fs182 and sarah-desktop-12 share IP 10.0.18.224 on\r\n  different subnets; it may be a mock artifact or an IP reassignment.\r\n"]
[12.130225, "x", "0"]
